// A body's size. `size` is a body register (state.body) holding the multiplier of the body's authored size: one at full
// size, a quarter after the Wonderland door (wonderland.puck), down to Alice's on the gallery's level 1, whose size field
// (gallery/building.puck's `gallerySizeField`) shrinks her on its stairs and in its lifts. `bodies.scale` names it, so
// the body's collider, speeds, gravity, step height, jump, reach, drawn form and chase camera follow it, and a crossing
// through a pair of two sizes or a size field's rule writes it. The register is the body's own, so it crosses with her
// through a painting: every world she can walk into imports this file and declares the same register, and she arrives
// the size she left in. The envelope is the world's own size range, a tenth to one, room under the smallest size a field
// authors; a crossing that would leave it is refused by name, and a size carried into a world is clamped to it. A world
// that stands a building at another scale widens it to that building's sizes (gallery/root.puck's `gallerySizeRange`).

state {
  body [
    {
      name: "size"
      kind: "Counter"
      initial: 1
      envelope {
        $type: "range"
        maximum: 1
        minimum: 0.1
      }
    }
  ]
}

bodies {
  scale: "size"
}
